candidates.evidence:
var elems = _.reduce(this, function(memo, elem) {
    return memo.concat(_.filter(elem.children, isTag));
  }, []);

candidates.body:
**Performance (medium)**: The `elems` array is built eagerly even when `selectorOrHaystack` is an object or node, causing unnecessary performance overhead.

```
var elems = _.reduce(this, function(memo, elem) {
    return memo.concat(_.filter(elem.children, isTag));
  }, []);
```

**Suggested fix:** Move the `if (selectorOrHaystack && typeof selectorOrHaystack !== 'string')` check to the very beginning of the function, before computing `elems`.

